
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Patient Admission Forecasting</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f2f5f9;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        header {
            background-color: #245b8f;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 25px;
        }

        .container {
            background-color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 20px auto;
            max-width: 800px;
            border-radius: 8px;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #245b8f;
        }

        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
        }

        th, td {
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            padding: 10px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        th {
            background-color: #245b8f;
            color: white;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 15px;
            color: #555;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Patient Admission Forecasting</h1>
        <p>A Machine Learning Mini Project</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
        <h2>About the Project</h2>
        <p>
            This project uses machine learning to predict future
            patient admissions based on historical admission data.
            It uses the Random Forest Regression algorithm to
            estimate the number of patients expected in upcoming days.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
        <h2>Technologies Used</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Python</li>
            <li>Pandas</li>
            <li>Scikit-learn</li>
            <li>Matplotlib</li>
            <li>Random Forest Regression</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
        <h2>Historical Admission Data</h2>

        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Day</th>
                <th>Patient Admissions</th>
            </tr>
            <tr><td>1</td><td>45</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2</td><td>48</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3</td><td>42</td></tr>
            <tr><td>4</td><td>50</td></tr>
            <tr><td>5</td><td>55</td></tr>
            <tr><td>6</td><td>53</td></tr>
            <tr><td>7</td><td>58</td></tr>
            <tr><td>8</td><td>60</td></tr>
            <tr><td>9</td><td>57</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10</td><td>65</td></tr>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
        <h2>Future Admission Forecast</h2>

        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Future Day</th>
                <th>Predicted Admissions</th>
            </tr>
            <tr><td>11</td><td>Forecast generated by Python model</td></tr>
            <tr><td>12</td><td>Forecast generated by Python model</td></tr>
            <tr><td>13</td><td>Forecast generated by Python model</td></tr>
        </table>

        <p>
            The predictions are generated using the trained
            Random Forest Regression model.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
        <h2>Model Evaluation</h2>
        <p>
            The model is evaluated using Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
            to measure the difference between actual and predicted
            admission numbers.
        </p>
    </div>

    <footer>
        <p>Patient Admission Forecasting | Machine Learning Project</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
